WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:14.340
CMake is often where a C++ team gathers compiler warnings, language standards, optimization settings, linker behavior, sanitizer profiles, and platform-specific hardening policy.

2
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.680
These choices should not be accidental.

3
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:24.780
They should be recorded in the build files, scoped to the targets and platforms that need them, and understandable to someone reviewing a change months later.

4
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.500
Warnings and diagnostics are part of quality control.

5
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:37.160
They catch questionable conversions, missing returns, shadowing, unused results, and other conditions that can become real defects.

6
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:51.900
A project does not need identical warning flags on every compiler, but it does need a consistent policy: important diagnostics are enabled, noisy exceptions are documented, and warning changes are reviewed as engineering decisions.

7
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.740
Sanitizer builds are another layer.

8
00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:03.960
Address, undefined behavior, thread, and leak sanitizer profiles help teams discover classes of defects during development and CI.

9
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:10.460
These profiles are not the same as release hardening, and they usually have different performance and runtime expectations.

10
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:17.680
Keeping them as named build profiles helps the team run them regularly without confusing them with production configuration.

11
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.680
Release hardening should be deliberate and verifiable.

12
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:32.220
Linker options, symbol visibility, stack protections, relocation settings, control-flow protections, and platform SDK choices all vary by compiler and operating system.

13
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:43.760
A maintainable CMake project expresses those choices in one reviewable policy area, applies them consistently, and confirms through logs or artifact inspection that the intended settings were actually used.
